# Vice Ops design (binding)

Before changing landing, shop, or customer UI, reuse these tokens — do not invent a new palette.

## Tokens

| Role | Token | Value |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Background | `night` / `--night` | `#0B0716` |
| Surface | `ink` | `#140E1C` |
| Text | `mist` / `--mist` | `#F4F0EA` |
| Muted text | `mute` / `--mute` | `#A89BA8` |
| Accent | `pink` / `--pink` | `#E85A9B` |
| Warm accent | `coral` / `--coral` | `#E8926A` |
| Cool accent | `teal` | `#7EC8C4` |
| Premium | `gold` | `#D4B483` |

Typography: Bebas (`font-display`) for display; Instrument Serif (`font-serif`) for editorial accents; DM Sans (`font-ui`) for body. Do not switch to Inter/Roboto/Arial.

## Spacing

Use a **4px scale** only: `4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32, 40, 48, 64…` (Tailwind `1` = 4px). Prefer existing section padding (`px-6` / `md:px-10`, `py-20` / `md:py-28`).

## Composition rules

- Landing first viewport: one composition — brand, one short line, one CTA group, one dominant background. No card grids or stat strips in the hero.
- No purple-on-white / indigo gradient soup. No cream+terracotta AI defaults. No hard black “mass” blobs behind the VI logo — neon glow + light depth only.
- Prefer hairline borders (`mist/10–25`) over heavy glass card stacks.
- Motion: spring/ease-out; one authored moment per section, not identical fades everywhere.

## Assets

Hero background: `/media/leonida-cityscape` (soft-blurred). Logo: `/media/vice-city-vi-logo.png` via `ViceCityLogo` (centered, spring hover). Do not reintroduce the old wordmark.
